      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test logic. It verifies that `withUseInput()` returns the same instance when the value is unchanged (identity preserved), and that the resulting value still reports `hasId()`. Let me write the improved version.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces auto-generated EvoSuite variable names (`object0`, `boolean0`, `jacksonInject_Value0/1`) with descriptive names (`injectionId`, `useInputEnabled`, `originalValue`, `valueAfterNoOpMutation`) and adds a Javadoc comment explaining the intent: verifying that `withUseInput()` returns the same instance when the value is already set to the given argument."
    }
